docs/paper/sections/results.tex-104-Exp\_008e\_v3 restricts imagination to $\dt{=}1$ while retaining the trained embedding. Two of four seeds collapse (50\%): Pathway~A (CIVO, $\nve = 4.02\times$) and preliminary Pathway~B (entropy \emph{increase}, $\nve = 3.78\times$; 2 seeds only, requires confirmation; see Figure~\ref{fig:multiple_pathways} in Appendix~\ref{sec:pathways}). Pathway~B produces one of three non-CIVO false positives ($n{=}30$).
docs/paper/sections/results.tex-105-\paragraph{F7: Full-pathway gradient stopping shows mixed results.}
docs/paper/sections/results.tex:106:Full-SGS (exp\_018) detaches all non-KL gradients from $e_{\dt}$. Seed~1 shows partial mitigation (eval 448.3, NVE $1.66\times$); seed~2 collapses (0/2 elimination; Appendix~\ref{sec:sgs_gradient_analysis}). Cross-environment validation on Cheetah (010b, NVE $8.27$--$108.52\times$) confirms CIVO generalization; full-SGS yields 0/3 elimination. Removing the embedding eliminates CIVO on Cheetah (024b, NVE $< 0.2\times$).
